From f9e312b0ce5c7fe1d224cb28dee14544298ec2ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:18:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Publishing plugins: send albums straight to a site
 (lionphotos-publish-v1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A plugin with kind "publish" sends albums and projects to a site that
speaks the publish protocol instead of exporting a page to a folder. The
export dialog asks for the site's address and an upload key, checks the
connection and publishes with the typed code; photos the site already
has are not sent again and the ones taken out of the album leave the
site. The key is kept encrypted by the system (safeStorage).

Adds the Coordenadoria de Comunicação UFSM (Mercúrio) plugin, texts in
the 10 languages, docs and unit checks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9hMzBG5JuzK7PLskYcV93
